  "summary": "Results inbox worked per RBC-INBOX-01, RBC-LAB-03 and RBC-RAD-05. 12 of 13 items closed. One is deliberately left open because no final report exists yet.\n\nOriginal 8 items:\n- pt-0006 Raj Patel, CT urogram (task-00001): no mass or stone found. The 4 mm LLL nodule is already followed in lung screening. Ordered the screening LDCT on the annual schedule (sr-t0001), with a tracking task, patient message and note. Later changed (see below).\n- pt-0016 TSH (task-00010): normal, closed.\n- pt-0016 potassium (task-00011): the lab corrected 6.3 to 4.4, which is normal. Closed with no action.\n- pt-0007 Leslie Parisian, preliminary CTA chest (task-00003): the final report dr-00084 replaces it. No PE and no nodule (the finding was a vessel); no follow-up needed. Closed.\n- pt-0007 BMP (task-00004): kidney injury. Creatinine rose from 0.98 to 1.64 within 48 h after IV contrast. Ordered an urgent repeat BMP by Mon 10/26 (sr-t0008), held naproxen, messaged the patient, created an RN call task due 10/26, wrote a note.\n- pt-0064 Helen Marchetti, creatinine 1.36 (task-64001): no earlier creatinine in the 7-day window, so it doesn't meet the kidney-injury rule. Closed.\n- pt-0033 Carol Whitfield, creatinine 1.31 (task-00025): the 10/21 value is entered in error and was not used. Rule not met against the 10/17 value of 1.27. Closed.\n- pt-0008 Walter Brennan, potassium 6.4 (task-00005): flagged hemolyzed at first. Ordered an urgent repeat BMP (sr-t0017), messaged the patient, wrote a note.\n\nArrivals while I worked (§8):\n- pt-0008: the lab corrected the result. The sample was not hemolyzed and 6.4 stands. Switched to the stat pathway: stat BMP today (sr-t0021, replaces sr-t0017), on-call pool notified at stat priority, medications reviewed (none raise potassium), corrected message asking the patient to come in today, addendum note. Closed.\n- pt-0033: new outside creatinine of 1.78, up from 1.31 nine hours earlier. This meets the kidney-injury rule. Ordered an urgent repeat BMP by 10/26 (sr-t0027), messaged the patient, wrote a note (flags hydrochlorothiazide, started 10/17). Closed.\n- pt-0064: new creatinine 1.48 with no earlier value in the window. No action; closed.\n- pt-0006: an addendum to the 4/14 screening scan found a new 5 mm RUL nodule (Lung-RADS 3, repeat scan in 6 months). Ordered the LDCT for 10/23–11/14 (sr-t0032) with a tracking task due 11/14, sent a corrected patient message, wrote an addendum note. Closed.\n- pt-0007 preliminary chest X-ray (inbox-a0002): possible 7 mm RUL nodule. Left open because no final report has been issued (§2c).\n\nNeeds your attention:\n1. The tools couldn't discontinue lab or imaging orders. The old orders sr-t0001 (pt-0006) and sr-t0017 (pt-0008) are still active but replaced by sr-t0032 and sr-t0021. task-t0034 asks you to discontinue sr-t0001 and close its old tracking task, task-t0002. For sr-t0017, only the note says it's replaced; no task was created.\n2. The portal message for pt-0007 says the final CTA found no nodule and no more lung imaging is needed. That still matches the final report, but check it once the chest X-ray is finalized.\n3. Six portal and pharmacy refill messages in your messages queue were outside this request and are still open.",
